{"name":"Autumn Spice","hex":"#d19957","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"autumn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Traditionally the third of the four seasons, when deciduous trees lose their leaves, and temperatures and daylight hours decrease; typically regarded as spanning the months of September, October, and November in the Northern Hemisphere, and the months of March, April and May in the Southern Hemisphere.","The time period when someone or something is past its prime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend the autumn (in a particular place).","To (cause to) undergo the changes associated with autumn, such as leaves changing color and falling from trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/autumn"},{"term":"spice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Aromatic or pungent plant matter (usually dried) used to season or flavor food.","The quality of being spicy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add spice or spices to; season.","To spice up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Autumn","blocks":[{"text":"Autumn, also known as fall in North American English, is one of the four temperate seasons on Earth. Outside the tropics, autumn marks the transition from summer to winter, beginning in September or March. Autumn is the season when the duration of daytime becomes noticeably shorter and the temperature cools considerably. Day length decreases and night length increases as the season progresses until the winter solstice in December and June. One of its main features in temperate climates is the striking change in colour of the leaves of deciduous trees as they prepare to shed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg/330px-D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autumn","wikidata":"Q1314"},{"title":"Spice","blocks":[{"text":"In the culinary arts, a spice is a seed, fruit, root, bark, or other plant substance primarily used for flavouring or colouring food. Spices are distinguished from herbs, which are the leaves, flowers, or stems of plants used for flavouring or as a garnish. Spices and herbs are both seasonings. \nSpices are sometimes used in medicine, religious rituals, cosmetics, or perfume production. They are usually classified into spices, spice seeds, and herbal categories. For example, vanilla is commonly used as an ingredient in fragrance manufacturing. Plant-based sweeteners such as sugar are not considered spices."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Spices1.jpg/330px-Spices1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spice","wikidata":"Q42527"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Quebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg/500px-Quebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Quebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg/1280px-Quebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Quebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg/500px-Quebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQuebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/J%C3%B3zef_Che%C5%82mo%C5%84ski_-_Jesie%C5%84_1875.jpg/500px-J%C3%B3zef_Che%C5%82mo%C5%84ski_-_Jesie%C5%84_1875.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimed